{"answer":"No supplied paper directly describes a method that finds relevant text chunks using a hierarchy of summaries to connect search terms and documents.

The closest themes are about adversarially perturbing or constraining model inputs: several papers formulate constrained or physics-informed adversaries that search within restricted sets or enforce constraints on perturbations (e.g., [3], [4], [5], [2]). Another related idea is geometry-aware or structured attacks that exploit hierarchical structure in embeddings (e.g., [6]), but these are not text-chunk retrieval with summary hierarchies.

If you can provide papers specifically about hierarchical summarization for information retrieval or chunk selection, I can try again.","grounded":false}
